s/suffixes signify different trade brands (e.g. \"New X\" is NOT \"X\", a brand ending in \"-rich\" is NOT \"-ren\"). Return \"no_match\".\r\n22:    - Allow common OCR scanning artifacts, dropped letters/syllables, phonetic variants, and Arabic/Persian letter substitutions of the SAME exact brand (e.g. فيوسيدين/فيوسيدل where connected 'ين' is read as 'ل', ميبو/ميو where 'ب' is dropped, جرانتريل/جرانتيل, امبوفير/اميفير, ديباكين/ديبيكان, or dropped initial 'ا', dropped single letters or missing dots like 'ن' or 'ب', Persian/Urdu letters like پ for ب or ک for ك or گ for ك/ج, visually confused OCR letters like 'ف' vs 'د', or slight vowel variations).\r\n23:    - EXACT BRAND CERTAINTY: If the primary trade brand word is identical on both sides, DO NOT doubt it, DO NOT suspect that it is a typo for a different drug, and DO NOT send it to \"review\" because of trade name doubt! Treat it as a 100% MATCH directly!\r\n24:    - BRAND PREFIX INTEGRITY: Different brand prefixes in single-word trade names (e.g. \"ابيكو-\" vs \"الـ-\" or distinct therapeutic prefixes) indicate completely different commercial brands. They MUST NEVER match (return \"no_match\").\r\n25: \r\n26: 2. DOSAGE FORM & FORMULATION (ZERO TOLERANCE FOR CONFLICTS):\r\n27:    - Dosage forms MUST be strictly compatible:\r\n28:      - Tablets/Capsules (اقراص, كبسول, حبوب, فيلم, شريط) ONLY match Tablets/Capsules.\r\n29:      - Syrups/Suspensions (شراب, شرب, معلق) ONLY match Syrups. NEVER match tablets with syrup.\r\n30:      - Creams (كريم) ONLY match Creams. NEVER match cream with ointment or suppository.\r\n31:      - Ointments (مرهم, دهان) ONLY match Ointments. Ointment and Cream are strictly different forms!\r\n32:      - Injections/Ampoules (امبول, حقن, فيال) ONLY match Injections.\r\n33:      - Suppositories (لبوس) ONLY match Suppositories.\r\n34:      - Drops (نقط, قطرة) ONLY match Drops. NEVER match drops with tablets or plain numbers without drops (e.g. كتافلام نقط does NOT match كتافلام 50).\r\n35:      -